---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for greek.tools — what data we collect, how we use it, and your rights."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl pb-12">
    <div class="mb-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--color-coral);">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-text-muted">Last updated: June 11, 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-policy">
      <p>
        This policy covers <a href="https://greek.tools">greek.tools</a> and{' '}
        <a href="https://hebrew.tools">hebrew.tools</a> (collectively, "the Sites"), operated by
        Mitchell Palermo.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>

      <p>
        <strong>Account information</strong><br />
        When you sign in with Google, we receive your name, email address, and profile picture. We
        store these to identify your account.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Study data</strong><br />
        We store your spaced repetition (SRS) card progress (scheduling intervals, due dates, review
        history), study statistics (streak, total reviews, accuracy), and any custom vocabulary decks
        you create. This data is linked to your account and synced across your devices.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Session data</strong><br />
        We store a session token along with your IP address and browser/device type (user agent
        string) to keep you signed in. Sessions expire after 30 days.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Analytics</strong><br />
        We use PostHog to collect page view counts, feature interaction events, and JavaScript error
        reports. PostHog records sessions for approximately 20% of visits to help us diagnose bugs.
        PostHog data is stored on servers in the United States.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Browser storage</strong><br />
        Before you sign in, study data is saved in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> and
        stays on your device. It is only uploaded to our servers when you explicitly sync.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To identify your account and keep you signed in</li>
        <li>To sync your study progress across devices</li>
        <li>To maintain your study streak and statistics</li>
        <li>To diagnose errors and improve the app</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not sell your data to third parties</li>
        <li>We do not use your data to serve advertisements</li>
        <li>We do not share your data with data brokers or advertising platforms</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Service</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Privacy policy</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Google</td>
            <td>Sign-in via OAuth</td>
            <td><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Cloudflare</td>
            <td>Hosting and database</td>
            <td
              ><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
                >cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a
              ></td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>PostHog</td>
            <td>Analytics and session recording</td>
            <td><a href="https://posthog.com/privacy">posthog.com/privacy</a></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        Your account and study data are retained for as long as your account is active. Session
        tokens expire after 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Account deletion</h2>
      <p>
        To delete your account and all associated data, contact us at{' '}
        <a href="mailto:hello@greek.tools">hello@greek.tools</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email{' '}
        <a href="mailto:hello@greek.tools">hello@greek.tools</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose-policy {
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .prose-policy p {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose-policy h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .prose-policy ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose-policy li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .prose-policy a {
    color: var(--color-coral);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .prose-policy a:hover {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .prose-policy code {
    font-size: 0.875em;
    background: var(--color-bg-card);
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .prose-policy table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .prose-policy th {
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-border, #e5e7eb);
  }

  .prose-policy td {
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border, #e5e7eb);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
</style>
